---
import Definition from '../../layouts/Definition.astro';
import Mermaid from '../../components/Mermaid.astro';
---

<Definition title="Splash Screen" section="Journey">
  <img slot="preview" src="/splash_screen.png" alt="PSZ Splash Screen" style="width:960px;height:540px;object-fit:contain;background:#000;" />

  <h2>Purpose</h2>
  <p>Godot's native boot splash. Displays the game logo on a black background while the engine initializes. This is rendered by the engine before any GDScript runs.</p>

  <h2>Behavior</h2>
  <p>Shown automatically by Godot on launch. Once the engine finishes initialization, it loads the main scene (<code>bootstrap.tscn</code>) which takes over with the <a href="/journey/download">Download Content</a> screen. The player always sees this transition — there is no skip path.</p>

  <Mermaid chart={`flowchart TD
    A[App Launch] --> B[Engine Boot Splash]
    B --> C[bootstrap.tscn loads]
    C --> D[Download Content screen]
  `} />

  <h2>Configuration</h2>
  <p>Set in <code>project.godot</code>:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>boot_splash/image</code> = <code>res://splash_screen.png</code></li>
    <li><code>boot_splash/bg_color</code> = black</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Next</h2>
  <p><a href="/journey/download">Download Content →</a></p>
</Definition>
